        <td>
          <p><b>Hi there, and welcome to my little corner of the World Wide Web!</b></p>
          <p>We are quietly handing a lot of human judgment over to machines &mdash; who
          gets hired, whose work is any good, what counts as honest, even how we learn. The
          question underneath my current work is what that does to us: when an algorithm
          steps into a decision we used to make ourselves, does it simply inherit our
          biases, or does it begin to reshape what we treat as fair, honest, and worth the
          effort? Grab a coffee, take a look at my working papers below, and enjoy your
          stay!</p>
        </td>
      </tr>
