    <!-- ~~~~~~~~ ABOUT ~~~~~~~~ -->
    <a name="about"></a>
    <h2 class="sec" id="about">About Me</h2>
    <p>I'm a behavioral economist, and since 2024 I hold the Chair of Behavioral Economics
    at WHU &ndash; Otto Beisheim School of Management. I use laboratory and field experiments
    to study the small moral moments that add up: when people bend the rules, how teams
    decide who's in and who's out, and how algorithms are starting to shape judgments we
    used to make on our own.</p>
    <p>I earned my doctorate in economics at the University of Cologne under Bernd Irlenbusch,
    and spent time along the way at Harvard's Program on Negotiation and at CREED in
    Amsterdam. Before taking up the chair, I was an assistant professor here at WHU.</p>

    <h3>My Education</h3>
    <ul class="retro">
      <li><b>2014</b> &mdash; Dr. rer. pol. (Economics), University of Cologne (advisor: Prof. Dr. Bernd Irlenbusch)</li>
      <li><b>2009</b> &mdash; Diploma in Economics, University of Bonn</li>
      <li><b>2003</b> &mdash; Abitur, Irmgardis-Gymnasium Cologne</li>
    </ul>

